{"name":"Shakshuka","hex":"#aa3311","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shakshuka","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Maghrebi dish of eggs simmered in a mixture of chopped tomatoes, chilies, cumin, peppers, and onions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shakshuka"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shakshouka","blocks":[{"text":"Shakshouka is a Maghrebi dish of eggs poached in a sauce of tomatoes, olive oil, peppers, onion, and garlic, commonly spiced with cumin, paprika, and cayenne pepper. Shakshouka is a popular dish throughout North Africa and the Middle East."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Shakshuka_by_Calliopejen1.jpg/330px-Shakshuka_by_Calliopejen1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shakshouka","wikidata":"Q2474644"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Shakshuka8.jpg/500px-Shakshuka8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Shakshuka8.jpg/1280px-Shakshuka8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Shakshuka8.jpg/500px-Shakshuka8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Individual portion of shakshouka","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShakshuka8.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Merguez_Shakshouka.jpg/500px-Merguez_Shakshouka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Merguez_Shakshouka.jpg/1280px-Merguez_Shakshouka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Merguez_Shakshouka.jpg/500px-Merguez_Shaks